      "writtenOn": "2014-05-27T00:02:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this should say for what operations. For example, it should say that it\u0027s for creating a user, updating a user to change the password, and changing a user\u0027s password.\n\nAlso, suggest change \"HTTP status 400 will be raised.\" to \"the operation will fail with a 403 Forbidden error.\"\n\nThe server should respond with a 403 error. 400 Bad Request indicates \"The request could not be understood by the server due to malformed syntax.\"  ( http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2616#section-10.4.1 ). In this case, the server understands the request and is refusing to do it ( http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2616#section-10.4.4 ).",
